    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d596">

                <pb facs="0595" n="591" sameAs="frus:frus1938v03/pg591"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/6762</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation by the Adviser on Political
                        Relations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hornbeck</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-12-20">December 20, 1938</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Under instruction by the Under Secretary, Mr. Welles, I made oral reply to Mr.
                    Mallet today. I said that I understood that the Treasury Department had been
                    talking with Mr. Bewley of the British Embassy in regard to the matter to which
                    this <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> refers and that I was under
                    instruction to say that the views of this Department coincided with the views
                    which the Treasury Department had expressed. I asked whether, in these premises,
                    this oral reply on our part would be satisfactory to the British Embassy. Mr.
                    Mallet said that it would and that he would report to his Government, as the
                    Department’s reply, what I had said.</p>
                <closer><signed>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">tanley</hi>] K. H[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ornbeck</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
